.TH QUOTA-REPORT 1 "October 2026" "SASD Freeware" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
quota-report \- query system filesystem quota utilities
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B quota-report
.RB [ --user " NAME" |
.BI --group " NAME" |
.BR --all ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Display the system quota report without modifying any quotas. With no option,
run quota -v for the current user. --user selects quota -v NAME,
--group selects quota -v -g NAME, and --all runs repquota -a.
Output is supplied by the native tool and remains platform-specific.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI --user " NAME"
Show quota for a named user.
.TP
.BI --group " NAME"
Show group quota, where supported by the system quota utility.
.TP
.B --all
Show the administrative report for all supported filesystems.
.TP
.B --help
Show usage.
.TP
.B --version
Show version.
.SH REQUIREMENTS
Perl 5.8 or newer and the system quota or repquota command.
The relevant filesystems must have quota support configured.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 native command succeeded; 2 invalid options;
3 required command missing or command execution failed.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR quota (1),
.BR repquota (8),
.BR fs-usage (1)
